    "visualSystem": "# Year 12 Physics M5 V18: Circular orbits. How does gravity maintain a circular orbit? (design)\n\nStatus: Revision 3 (13 Nov 2026): visual-standard top-up (stage list, question-card pictures, givens strips, five-line notes, simulation engines named, root rules R1 to R4), visuals only. Narration unchanged. Needs a Codex error check before plates and voicing. Previously Revision 2 (6 Nov 2026): brief 188 findings resolved and visual upgrade to maths-visual-standard.md.\n\nNarration 5,727 characters (scene sum; Revision 1 stated 5,606 by the joined convention), 17 scenes, about 514 s, counted by script with the build parser rules (see \"Narration length estimate\").\n\nScope: Year 12 Physics (Physics Stage 6, 2017 syllabus), Module 5 (Advanced Mechanics), inquiry question \"How does the force of gravity determine the motion of planets and satellites?\". Templates as `phys-y12-m5-v17.md`. No pre-design pack exists; the pack work is done here. Site lessons read in full (6 Nov, read-only): `C:/Users/kygs/teaching-app-fix/subjects/physics/year12/module5/lesson11.sa.html`, SHA256 `62b7d2be3790b2adf89c177e71c4be0b7af850d8005f56cdd75c2f88c441ef3e` (stale: hashed against the old C:/Users/kygs/hscscience copy; not re-hashed against teaching-app-fix, 24 Nov 2026), and `.../module5/lesson17.sa.html`, SHA256 `01842919fdfa6884fe4144bf4197bb53f8d91c2f43873464c113dadcc13b8f8e` (both recomputed 6 Nov; both match the route). Route entry: `phys-y12-m5-v18`. Route start: \"Start from the physical case in the learner question; recall only the earlier result needed for it.\" Route stop: \"Equate gravitational resultant with centripetal requirement, deriving v=sqrt(GM/r) and period relation. Stop before ellipse dynamics.\" Next: \"phys-y12-m5-v19: What makes an orbit geostationary rather than merely near Earth?\"\n\nOwner rules applied: as v17 (2017 syllabus quoted exactly; no people, hands, faces or body outlines: Newton is named, not drawn; the space station is shown